# Context Constraints

- Keep context thin, curated, and referential.
- Record provenance for concrete repository claims where practical.
- Do not store secrets, credentials, production data, or raw chat transcripts.
- Do not mirror source code, migrations, contracts, generated graph/index data, test dumps, or build artifacts.
- Preserve pre-existing uncommitted work in every member repository.
- Treat generated semantic and graph evidence as disposable and rebuildable.
- Promote durable validated technical decisions into their canonical owning ADR, contract, specification, or documentation.
